"light\":\"#C7F284\",\"dark\":\"#000000\"},\"logo\":{\"light\":\"https://mintcdn.com/jupiter/mrenEfoqnubhOTHf/logo/logo.png?fit=max\u0026auto=format\u0026n=mrenEfoqnubhOTHf\u0026q=85\u0026s=e745e60a4186bc382d3d5d9bdff9273a\",\"dark\":\"https://mintcdn.com/jupiter/mrenEfoqnubhOTHf/logo/logo.png?fit=max\u0026auto=format\u0026n=mrenEfoqnubhOTHf\u0026q=85\u0026s=e745e60a4186bc382d3d5d9bdff9273a\",\"href\":\"https://developers.jup.ag/\"},\"favicon\":\"https://mintcdn.com/jupiter/mrenEfoqnubhOTHf/favicon.png?fit=max\u0026auto=format\u0026n=mrenEfoqnubhOTHf\u0026q=85\u0026s=453e41111d621d16c4f196f9e772ce58\",\"api\":{\"playground\":{\"display\":\"interactive\"}},\"appearance\":\"$18:2:props:children:1:props:appearance\",\"navbar\":{\"primary\":{\"type\":\"button\",\"label\":\"Dashboard\",\"href\":\"https://developers.jup.ag/portal\"}},\"footer\":{\"socials\":{\"x\":\"https://x.com/JupiterExchange\",\"discord\":\"https://discord.gg/jup\",\"telegram\":\"https://t.me/jup_dev\",\"github\":\"https://github.com/jup-ag\",\"youtube\":\"https://www.youtube.com/@JupiterOnchain\"},\"links\":[{\"items\":[{\"label\":\"Support\",\"href\":\"/docs/resources/support\"},{\"label\":\"Guidelines\",\"href\":\"/docs/legal\"},{\"label\":\"Legal\",\"href\":\"/docs/legal/sdk-api-license-agreement\"},{\"label\":\"Brand Kit\",\"href\":\"/docs/resources/brand-kit\"},{\"label\":\"Status\",\"href\":\"https://status.jup.ag\"}]}]},\"seo\":{\"metatags\":{\"og:title\":\"Jupiter Developers\",\"og:description\":\"Build with the most comprehensive set of APIs, tool kits, and technical deep dives across Jupiter's full product suite - Swap, Lend, Perps, and beyond.\",\"og:image\":\"/logo/og.png\",\"og:type\":\"website\",\"og:url\":\"https://developers.jup.ag/\",\"og:site_name\":\"Jupiter Developers\",\"description\":\"Build with the most comprehensive set of APIs, tool kits, and technical deep dives across Jupiter's full product suite - Swap, Tokens, Price, Lend, Spot, and beyond.\",\"keywords\":\"Jupiter, Jupiter Developer Documentation, Jupiter API, Jupiter SDK, Jupiter Swap, Jupiter Lend, Jupiter Perps, Jupiter Studio, Jupiter Tool Kits, Jupiter Plugin, Jupiter Wallet Kit, Jupiter Referral Program, Jupiter Routing, Solana, Crypto, Solana Swap, Crypto Swap, Jupiter Utlra\",\"twitter:card\":\"summary_large_image\",\"twitter:site\":\"@JupiterExchange\",\"twitter:title\":\"Jupiter Developers\",\"twitter:description\":\"Build with the most comprehensive set of APIs, tool kits, and technical deep dives across Jupiter's full product suite - Swap, Lend, Perps, and beyond.\",\"twitter:image\":\"/logo/og.png\"}},\"banner\":{\"content\":\"Manage your API keys, billing, and usage on the [**Developer Platform**](https://developers.jup.ag/portal). Questions? Reach us via [**Support**](/docs/resources/support).\"},\"contextual\":{\"options\":[\"copy\",\"view\",\"chatgpt\",\"claude\",\"cursor\",\"vscode\"],\"display\":\"header\"},\"styling\":{\"latex\":true,\"codeblocks\":\"system\"},\"navigation\":{\"pages\":[]}},\"docsNavWithMetadata\":\"$undefined\",\"anonymizedNav\":\"$undefined\",\"hasFullNav\":false},\"children\":\"$L2d\"}]}]}]}]]}]]}]]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2f:T4ad,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"How to use the Jupiter Developer Platform firewall to control traffic to API keys used in browser, mobile, or other client-side apps. Firewall rules are evaluated per team at the api.jup.ag gateway before requests reach the API, with up to 50 rules per team (enabled or disabled, deleted rules excluded). When several rules match a request, one decision rule wins by: (1) action precedence Bypass \u003e Deny \u003e Rate limit \u003e Log, (2) specificity (count of distinct condition types in the matched group, e.g. path + country = 2 beats path alone = 1), (3) age (older rule wins). Each rule combines conditions (Path starts-with prefix, API keys is-any-of, Method, Country, Header, IP/CIDR) with AND/OR groups and one of four actions: Log (record only), Deny (returns 403 'Request blocked by firewall'), Rate limit (N requests per second/minute scoped per IP, per API key, or per team; returns 429 when exceeded), or Bypass (skips firewall checks for matching trusted traffic, must have at least one condition). Each rule shows a human-readable IF...THEN Expression Overview. Firewall decisions and matched rules appear in request logs and Firewall analytics, and rule changes are recorded in the audit log."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"19:[\"$\",\"$L2e\",null,{\"scopedNav\":{\"global\":null,\"tabs\":[{\"tab\":\"Get Started\",\"groups\":[{\"group\":\"Get Started\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Jupiter Developer Docs\",\"sidebarTitle\":\"Welcome to Jupiter\",\"description\":\"DeFi infrastructure on Solana for swaps, lending, limit orders, DCA, and more\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Welcome page for Jupiter Developer Docs. Introduces Jupiter as Solana DeFi infrastructure and provides quick navigation to product APIs (Swap, Tokens, Price, Lend, LO \u0026 DCA, Prediction, Perps), developer resources (Guides, API Reference, Developer Platform), AI resources (CLI, Skills, MCP, llms.txt), community links, socials (Blog and X), and get-started setup pages.\",\"href\":\"/get-started\"},{\"title\":\"Environment Setup\",\"description\":\"Install required libraries, configure an RPC connection, and set up a development wallet.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Install Solana web3.js and spl-token libraries, configure an RPC connection, and set up a development wallet to build with the Jupiter API.\",\"href\":\"/get-started/environment-setup\"},{\"title\":\"Development Basics\",\"description\":\"Solana fundamentals for Jupiter developers: accounts, programs, transactions, priority fees, and how the Swap API simplifies it all.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Solana fundamentals for Jupiter developers: accounts, programs, instructions, transactions, priority fees, compute units, slippage, and how the Swap API V2 simplifies it all. Use the /order + /execute path for managed execution (no RPC needed) or /build for custom transactions.\",\"href\":\"/get-started/development-basics\"},{\"title\":\"Developer Guides\",\"sidebarTitle\":\"Guides\",\"description\":\"How-to guides for building on Solana with Jupiter.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Jupiter developer guides: practical tutorials for common Solana development tasks. Covers token swaps with Swap API V2 /order (recommended, two API calls, no RPC needed), token information (metadata, verification, organic score), token prices (USD pricing), swap widget embedding (Plugin), custom swap transactions with Swap API V2 /build (routing, CPI, custom instructions), and prediction markets (binary event trading). Each guide includes working code examples in JavaScript, Python, and curl.\",\"href\":\"/guides/index\"}]},{\"group\":\"Portal\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Getting Started\",\"description\":\"Set up your Jupiter API key and start building.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"How to get started with the Jupiter Developer Platform: sign up, create or join a team, generate an API key scoped to that team, and make your first request. API key is passed via x-api-key header; new keys take effect within about 15 seconds. Four tiers available: Free (1 RPS), Developer ($25/mo, 10 RPS), Launch ($100/mo, 50 RPS), Pro ($500/mo, 150 RPS). Keyless access available at 0.5 RPS without sign-up.\",\"href\":\"/portal/setup\"},{\"group\":\"Plans \u0026 Limits\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Plans and Pricing\",\"description\":\"Choose a plan that fits your project - from free to enterprise.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Jupiter Developer Platform pricing tiers: Free (1 RPS, no payment), Developer ($25/mo, 10 RPS, 25M credits), Launch ($100/mo, 50 RPS, 100M credits), Pro ($500/mo, 150 RPS, 500M credits). Overage billing applies to usage beyond included credits. Per-endpoint credit costs vary from 0 (execute endpoints) to 100 (portfolio positions). Keyless access available at 0.5 RPS.\",\"href\":\"/portal/plans\"},{\"title\":\"Rate Limits\",\"description\":\"Rate limits for Jupiter APIs by plan tier.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Jupiter API rate limits by plan tier: Keyless 0.5 RPS, Free 1 RPS, Developer 10 RPS, Launch 50 RPS, Pro 150 RPS. All tiers use a 60-second sliding window. Rate limits apply per organisation, not per API key. Most API requests share the main rate limit bucket, but /swap/v2/execute has its own dedicated bucket separate from the main limit: Keyless 20 RPS, Free 50 RPS, Paid (Developer/Launch/Pro) 100 RPS. Rate-limited responses include x-ratelimit-remaining, x-ratelimit-current, and x-ratelimit-reset headers (on successful and 429 responses, not on 401/403). Firewall rules can impose additional per-IP, per-API-key, or per-team limits on top of the plan limit. Returns HTTP 429 when exceeded.\",\"href\":\"/portal/rate-limits\"}]},{\"group\":\"Platform Features\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Organisations \u0026 Teams\",\"description\":\"Group your teams under one organisation, each with its own keys, analytics, and logs.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"How organisations and teams work in the Jupiter Developer Platform. An organisation groups teams; each team has its own API keys, analytics, request logs, and firewall rules, so you can separate products or environments. Each team has a slug (lowercase a-z, 0-9, hyphens, max 48 chars, unique per organisation) used in its Portal URL /portal/{org}/{team}. An organisation has three roles: owner, admin, and member; team membership is separate and binary. All organisation members can view every team's analytics and logs read-only. Managing a team's API keys and firewall rules requires membership of that team or an owner/admin role in the organisation. Managing billing and the plan requires an owner or admin role. An organisation can have multiple owners; an existing owner promotes another member to owner, and the original owner keeps their role unless they voluntarily self-demote. The last remaining owner cannot be demoted or removed. Members are invited by email and invitations expire after 10 days.\",\"href\":\"/portal/organisations\"},{\"title\":\"API Keys\",\"description\":\"Create API keys, restrict them to specific APIs, and manage their lifecycle.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"How to create and manage Jupiter Developer Platform API keys and restrict them with permissions. Keys are created inside a team, use the format jup_..., need a name unique within the team, and are shown in full only at creation (afterwards only the first and last few characters appear). Pass a key in the x-api-key header to api.jup.ag. New keys, permission changes, and deletions take effect within about 15 seconds. By default a key can call every Jupiter API. Permissions are an allow-list of products matched by case-sensitive path prefix, across Swap (which also covers /tx/v1/submit), Tokens, Price, Trigger, Recurring, Portfolio, Lend, Send, Studio, and Prediction. Once a list is set, the key can only call those endpoints, and a request to a disallowed endpoint is rejected at the gateway with 403 Forbidden and the message 'API key does not have access to this endpoint'. Covers the lifecycle (create, view, delete), permissions, and best practices: one key per app or environment, least privilege, and rotation.\",\"href\":\"/portal/api-keys\"},{\"title\":\"Firewall\",\"description\":\"Set rules to limit, rate-limit, or block traffic to your API keys at the gateway.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"$2f\",\"href\":\"/portal/firewall\"},{\"title\":\"Request Logs\",\"description\":\"Inspect individual requests to debug an integration and see what the gateway did.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"How to use the Jupiter Developer Platform request logs to inspect individual requests to api.jup.ag. Logs are scoped to a team, listed newest first, with cursor-based pagination, and can be filtered by status code, method, API group, and path. Selecting a request opens a detail panel with the full record, including the firewall decision. Each entry records: timestamp, request ID, client IP, ASN, country, host, referrer, user-agent, method, URI path and query, HTTP status, bytes sent and received, credits consumed, a latency breakdown (total, auth, time to first byte, time to last byte), and the firewall outcome with the rules that matched. Request logs are retained for 6 months.\",\"href\":\"/portal/logs\"},{\"title\":\"Analytics\",\"description\":\"Understand your traffic, performance, cost, and origin, per team and per API.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"How to read the Jupiter Developer Platform analytics for a team. A timezone-aware period picker (which persists as you navigate) controls the range; the time bucket scales with the range (up to 1h = 1 minute, up to 1 day = 15 minutes, up to 7 days = 6 hours, up to 30 days = 12 hours, over 30 days = 1 day). Overview KPIs, each with a period-over-period trend: total requests, errors and error rate (4xx or 5xx responses as a percentage of total requests), latency p50/p95/p99, and credits consumed. Charts: requests, latency, credits over time, status-code distribution, geographic distribution, and top paths. A per-API breakdown shows latency p50/p90/p99 and request and error counts per API. Some APIs have deeper analytics (volume, success rate, phase latency, top token pairs, fees collected). Firewall analytics: outcomes over time and rule-match counts. Analytics cover the last 6 months.\",\"href\":\"/portal/analytics\"},{\"title\":\"Account Security\",\"description\":\"Protect your account with two-factor authentication and review activity in the audit log.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"How to secure a Jupiter Developer Platform account and review activity. Two-factor authentication (2FA) supports an authenticator app (TOTP), email one-time codes, and backup recovery codes; 2FA applies only to email and password sign-in, OAuth sign-in is not covered by it, and accounts that only use OAuth cannot enable 2FA. The audit log records 17 event types across API keys (created, deleted, renamed), plan (changed, subscribed), payments (succeeded, failed), members (invited, removed, role changed, left), invitation canceled, and firewall rules (created, updated, enabled, disabled, deleted). The audit log can be filtered by event type. Most events are retained for 1 year; payment events are retained for 7 years; sensitive metadata is redacted.\",\"href\":\"/portal/security\"}]},{\"group\":\"Reference\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Response Codes\",\"description\":\"HTTP response codes for Jupiter APIs.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Common HTTP response codes from Jupiter APIs: 200 success, 400 bad request, 401 unauthorized (only when an invalid or unknown API key is sent; a request with no x-api-key header is treated as keyless), 403 forbidden (message 'API key does not have access to this endpoint' for permission denial, or 'Request blocked by firewall' for a firewall deny rule), 404 not found, 429 rate limited (message '[API Gateway] Too many requests' for plan limit, or 'Too many requests' for a firewall rate-limit rule), and 5xx server errors, with debugging guidance.\",\"href\":\"/portal/responses\"},{\"title\":\"Latency and Server Locations\",\"description\":\"API gateway regions and colocation guidance for lowest latency\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Jupiter's API gateway server locations and colocation guidance for integrators optimising latency. The API gateway runs on AWS in six regions: Singapore (ap-southeast-1), Frankfurt (eu-central-1), Virginia (us-east-1), São Paulo (sa-east-1), Tokyo (ap-northeast-1), and Oregon (us-west-2). Covers how to choose the closest region for your servers, general colocation recommendations, and how latency varies by proximity. Applies to all Jupiter API products accessed via api.jup.ag and lite-api.jup.ag.\",\"href\":\"/portal/latency\"},{\"title\":\"Migrating to Developer Platform\",\"description\":\"How to migrate from the old Jupiter Portal to the new Developer Platform.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Migration guide from the old Jupiter Portal to the new Developer Platform. Covers legacy organisation setup, API key preservation, tier mapping (Free/Pro/Ultra to new Free/Developer/Launch/Pro tiers), grace period with equivalent rate limits, billing transition to Stripe, and Lite API phase-out. No breaking changes to the API itself.\",\"href\":\"/portal/migration\"},{\"title\":\"FAQ\",\"description\":\"Frequently asked questions about the Jupiter Developer Platform.\",\"llmsDescription\":\"Frequently asked questions about the Jupiter Developer Platform: plan differences, API key usage and permissions, who can see a team's data and keys, stopping a leaked key from being abused, rate-limiting by country or IP with firewall rules, billing, upgrades and downgrades, credit overages, migration from old Portal, and support channels.\",\"href\":\"/portal/faq\"}]}]}]},{\"tab\":\"Docs\",\"menu\":[{\"item\":\"Swap\",\"icon\":\"arrow-right-arrow-left\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Swap\",\"href\":\"/swap\"}]},{\"item\":\"Tokens\",\"icon\":\"coin\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Tokens\",\"href\":\"/tokens\"}]},{\"item\":\"Price\",\"icon\":\"dollar-sign\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Price\",\"href\":\"/price\"}]},{\"item\":\"Transaction Landing\",\"icon\":\"paper-plane\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Transaction Landing\",\"href\":\"/transaction/submit\"}]},{\"item\":\"JupUSD\",\"icon\":\"money-bill\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"JupUSD\",\"href\":\"/jupusd\"}]},{\"item\":\"Lend\",\"icon\":\"piggy-bank\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Lend\",\"href\":\"/lend\"}]},{\"item\":\"LO \u0026 DCA\",\"icon\":\"crosshairs\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"LO \u0026 DCA\",\"href\":\"/trigger\"}]},{\"item\":\"Prediction\",\"icon\":\"check-to-slot\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Prediction\",\"href\":\"/prediction\"}]},{\"item\":\"More\",\"icon\":\"ellipsis\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"More\",\"href\":\"/portfolio\"}]}],\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Docs\",\"href\":\"/swap\"}]},{\"tab\":\"AI\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"AI\",\"href\":\"/ai\"}]},{\"tab\":\"Tool Kits\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Tool Kits\",\"href\":\"/tool-kits\"}]},{\"tab\":\"Changelog\",\"href\":\"https://developers.jup.ag/changelog\"},{\"tab\":\"Resources\",\"pages\":[{\"title\":\"Resources\",\"href\":\"/resources/support\"}]}]},\"maps\":{\"firstHrefInVersion\":{},\"firstHrefInLanguage\":{}},\"children\":\"$L30\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"31:I[604804,[\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/19ae1768f166fab9.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/b664fc8bb1e7ab0d.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/94ba86e1fd784047.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/72d5764206b37924.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/f4f18ea5f53bd0c5.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/c4608cfd78b1c60b.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/81b2abcf9f67bd98.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/a919d558158c76f7.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/4107fd9943c6bf0a.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/a8f237047ee4e827.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/9dbdcac3adf7f627.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/4b97f384bc2bdc55.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/254024bb2b699673.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/c7c9dfd26f25e785.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/185d26c1cc9dbd3c.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/f26ebb85d802f5a5.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\"],\"LoginButtonProvider\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"32:I[141180,[\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/19ae1768f166fab9.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6uW\",\"/docs/_next/static/chunks/b664fc8bb1e7ab0d.js?dpl=dpl_CS1yoCQzWRFY7R2gvmjD3jmnD6